a greek coast guard boat arrives in  corfu harbour on board is a passenger  rescued from the euro ferry olympia  which caught fire on friday  the 21 year old truck driver from  belarus told rescuers he'd heard the  voices of other passengers as he escaped  from his cabin to the upper deck of the  ferry he's now recovering in hospital  this morning we had very good news a 21  year old belarusian citizen came to our  hospital he was in very good shape he  underwent medical examinations he was  rehydrated and went through additional  tests  his rescue has renewed hopes that other  missing passengers may still be alive  this woman's come to the port hoping to  hear news about her husband  he's alive he's a professional he's very  experienced and capable and he's alive  i'm telling you with certainty action  has to be taken immediately how much  longer can all those people in there  bear it  these passengers were some of the first  to be rescued from the burning ferry  arriving home in italy they said they  were traumatized by what they'd  experienced  it wasn't easy i'm a strong person used  to fighting but this time the fear was  great  when you start to see the smoke and you  can't breathe anymore and people are  falling to the ground small children a  situation like that you can't understand  unless you've lived it  firefighters boarded the ferry for the  first time on sunday morning they'd been  delayed by temperatures of up to 600  degrees celsius  tugboats have now secured the vessel but  the authorities are worried whether  conditions may deteriorate further  hampering the rescue operation  victoria gatenby al jazeera
 

